# CI budgets II (docs/steps/ci-budgets-2/answered.md): a Windows session's
# open made cheaper at its cause, and the tests that run it made cheaper.

# --------------------------------------- the walk's look at a name, on Windows

[break] walk-takes-a-reparse-point-for-a-plain-name
rule: On Windows the walk takes a name for no link from its attributes only when they show no reparse point; a reparse point (a link, a junction) is looked at by `symlink_metadata`, which tells a link by its tag, and is followed by the walk itself.
file: crates/cineris-base/src/path/resolve.rs
in: is_link
find: Ok(attributes) if !attributes.is_reparse_point() => return Ok(false),
replace: Ok(_) => return Ok(false),
os: windows
caught-by:
    cineris-base::it paths_windows::sys_a_junction_that_leaves_the_workspace_resolves_outside
    cineris-base::it paths_windows::a_directory_link_that_leaves_the_workspace_resolves_outside

[break] walk-reads-a-directory-from-the-wrong-attribute
rule: On Windows a name with no reparse point is a directory when its attributes say so.
file: crates/cineris-base/src/path/resolve.rs
in: is_dir
find: return attributes.is_directory();
replace: return !attributes.is_directory();
os: windows
caught-by:
    cineris-base::it paths::the_workspace_must_be_an_existing_directory
    cineris-base::it paths::a_trailing_separator_names_a_directory
